r=Path.cwd();p=r/'tools/build-guides.py';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig')
user=[
'Open the intended project or cache and choose Database schema in the upper-right page selector. Choose procedure, function or trigger in the kind selector, then declared stored object in the state selector. Select a row. A procedure groups database work, a function declares a returned value and a trigger associates work with a database event. DPH inspects already captured SQL resources; it does not execute the selected application or SQL.',
'The details memo begins with the stored-object name, captured CREATE operation, language, return type and ordered parameters. Each parameter shows position, exact name, IN/OUT/INOUT or supported output mode, declared type, default text and source line. Literal default values are replaced with a literal-omitted marker. Not declared means absent from the captured statement, not an engine default or proof that a value cannot be returned.',
'For a trigger, read Trigger table, Timing, Events, Scope and WHEN before the body. BEFORE, AFTER and INSTEAD OF describe captured timing; they are not observations of an execution. A supported trigger can retain an inline block or an explicit zero-argument function call. WHEN remains unevaluated text. Unsupported event or option grammar stays in an explained gap.',
'Scroll the command strip sideways to the relationship selector, choose a table reference, procedure call, trigger table or function call, then click Follow relationship. DPH clears the filters and selects the exact captured target on its required 250-row page. Missing or ambiguous definitions have no guessed link. Multiple definitions and overloads remain independent; a name match cannot establish runtime argument binding or which migration is effective.',
'The captured body appears after the structural facts and relationship notes. Comments and string literals are omitted, including literals inside supported single-quoted or dollar-quoted SQL bodies. The original attached source or cache remains unchanged. Open source requires the current attached capture generation and unchanged source hash; detached or changed source produces an explanation instead of opening unverified live content.',
'Dependency coverage is deliberately qualified. Supported literal table references and explicit calls provide evidence links. Dynamic execution, expression calls, aliases, CTE binding and column binding remain unverified; table references in a body containing WITH stay unresolved. Empty dependencies do not establish independence. Display is bounded to 1000 dependencies per object and 10000 across the projection; a reached limit is explained. These are source relationships, not observed execution paths.',
'Search accepts object name, source, language, return type, trigger event/timing, parameter text or sanitized body text. First page resets pagination; Next page shows the next 250 matches. For a practice session and exact launch/build directions, use docs/guides/Database_Stored_Objects_Run_and_Test.txt. In the controlled fixture Data.Save has ordered parameters and links to Data.Target, Data.Log and Page270. Data.Audit links its event table and Data.Hook function. MissingRef, DynamicRef and AmbiguousHook demonstrate evidence gaps.'
]
engineering=[
'TDPHDatabaseSchema.Inspect projects supported stored-object declarations from existing captured SQL IR into procedure, function and trigger rows. CREATE, CREATE OR REPLACE and CREATE OR ALTER retain their header operation; PROC normalizes to procedure. Explicit qualified and quoted names are retained without dialect case folding. Named parenthesized parameters and supported TSQL @parameter lists retain order, modes, declared type, sanitized defaults and source lines. Scalar/qualified type structure, numeric precision, supported multiword types and array suffixes are captured; unsupported structures remain extraction gaps.',
'Inline BEGIN/END blocks retain internal semicolons and nested BEGIN/CASE structure, with a 128 nesting limit. Their internal DDL is never promoted to a top-level table declaration. An unterminated block holds the remaining resource as a gap. Standalone GO client batch separators preserve following declarations. Single-quoted and dollar-quoted SQL or PLPGSQL bodies are lexed again for sanitized display and supported dependency evidence; comments and literal values remain omitted. Other quoted-body languages, unsupported tails, unnamed parameters, table-valued return structure and custom terminator directives remain gaps. Capturing a supported header/body extent does not validate body grammar.',
'Trigger structure retains supported BEFORE/AFTER/INSTEAD OF timing, INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/TRUNCATE event lists, ON table, optional FOR EACH ROW/STATEMENT and parenthesized WHEN text. Supported bodies are inline blocks or explicit zero-argument EXECUTE FUNCTION/PROCEDURE calls; the latter names a trigger function. Other trigger dialect arrangements or call arguments remain explicit extraction gaps. Body text and WHEN are unevaluated.',
'Dependency extraction records supported FROM/JOIN/UPDATE and INSERT INTO literal table names, CALL/EXEC and EXECUTE PROCEDURE targets, plus event tables and explicit trigger functions. It is textual evidence with exact source lines, not a complete semantic SQL dependency graph. CTE/WITH scope, dynamic execution and complex table expressions retain unresolved evidence. No alias, expression-function call or column binding is invented. Projection-wide limits are 1000 dependency entries per stored object and 10000 total, alongside existing 2 MiB resource, 100000-token and 10000-row limits. Body display is limited to approximately 16000 characters and definition display to approximately 8000.',
'ResolveStored builds multiplicity indexes for captured table/view names and kind-specific routine names. Unique exact name matches receive target IDs with binding explicitly unverified. Missing or ambiguous declarations and overloads receive states without targets. Duplicate definitions remain separate and effective migration order remains unknown. Stored rows carry resource SHA256, generation, statement line and resource byte extent; parameter/dependency lines refer to that same captured resource. The captured workspace, source files and owner catalog remain unchanged.',
'The IDE-editable Database schema selectors add procedure/function/trigger and declared stored object. Existing exact-ID Follow relationship, paging, labeled scrolling details and source hash/generation guards are reused. Search includes parameter JSON text, language, returns, trigger facts and sanitized body. No runtime controls, driver connections, server SQL execution or new helper unit are introduced.',
'Run tools/build-database-stored-objects.cmd elevated for actual project/resource capture, parameters/defaults/types, quoted bodies, triggers, nested blocks, explicit calls, missing/ambiguous targets, overloads, literal omission, limits, batch boundaries, persistence, unchanged source/catalog/workspace, source guards and native navigation/filter/replacement/normal/compact renders. Run index and schema regressions and tools/build-wp0.cmd for the actual application and FMX resource bindings. Controlled fixtures stay in fixed ignored bin/database-stored-objects-validation.',
'Primary syntax references: PostgreSQL CREATE FUNCTION https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/sql-createfunction.html, CREATE TRIGGER https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/sql-createtrigger.html and Microsoft CREATE PROCEDURE https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/t-sql/statements/create-procedure-transact-sql. The parser implements a bounded captured-evidence subset; these references do not imply full dialect validation or deployed behavior.'
]
